Subject: Skip __STDC_ISO_10646__ wchar_t error guard on Linux
Policy-Class: P2-Package
Rationale: musl-based Linux toolchains (including Fil-C usermusl) use Unicode wchar_t without defining __STDC_ISO_10646__, causing src/chartype.h to abort compilation unless __linux__ is excluded alongside macOS and the BSDs.
Upstream-Status: Pending
Fil-C-Origin-Commits: cede3de02b42

diff --git a/src/chartype.h b/src/chartype.h
--- a/src/chartype.h
+++ b/src/chartype.h
@@ -39,7 +39,8 @@
 	!(defined(__APPLE__) && defined(__MACH__)) && \
 	!defined(__OpenBSD__) && \
 	!defined(__FreeBSD__) && \
-	!defined(__DragonFly__)
+	!defined(__DragonFly__) && \
+	!defined(__linux__)
 #ifndef __STDC_ISO_10646__
 /* In many places it is assumed that the first 127 code points are ASCII
  * compatible, so ensure wchar_t indeed does ISO 10646 and not some other
